@startuml crdt-convergence
' State-based CvRDT convergence: three replicas of a grow-only set (G-Set) exchange states by gossip and
' merge with join (= ∪). Because ⊔ is idempotent, commutative, and associative, every replica that has
' seen the same updates converges to the IDENTICAL state — regardless of order, duplication, or batching.
' Render:  plantuml -tsvg crdt-convergence.puml     Tool: PlantUML (uml_architecture, sequence diagram).

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName "DejaVu Sans"
skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1.1
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam participant {
  BackgroundColor #DBEAFE
  BorderColor #1E3A8A
}
skinparam sequence {
  LifeLineBorderColor #93C5FD
  LifeLineBackgroundColor #EFF6FF
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #EDE9FE
  BorderColor #5B21B6
}
autonumber

participant "Replica 1" as R1
participant "Replica 2" as R2
participant "Replica 3" as R3

note over R1,R3: each replica holds a G-Set, merged by join = ∪
R1 -> R1: local add → {alice}
R2 -> R2: local add → {bob, carol}
R3 -> R3: local add → {alice, bob}
R2 -> R1: gossip {bob, carol}
R1 -> R1 #86EFAC: join → {alice, bob, carol}
R3 -> R1: gossip {alice, bob}\n(overlaps — idempotent)
R1 -> R1: join → {alice, bob, carol}\n(no change)
R1 -> R3: gossip {alice, bob, carol}
R3 -> R3 #86EFAC: join → {alice, bob, carol}
note over R1,R3: any order / duplication / batching → identical state ✓ (convergence)
@enduml
